{
  "source": "/Users/russellcollis/Documents/GitHub/Teams Backgrounds/Teams Backgrounds/SigningHelpView.swift",
  "tables": {
    "Localizable": [
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Finding Your Developer ID",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 22,
          "startingLine": 10
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Signing the PKG with a **Developer ID Installer** certificate lets Gatekeeper and your MDM (Intune, Jamf, …) verify who built it and that it hasn't been changed. Signing is optional, but unsigned packages are blocked when opened from a download.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 22,
          "startingLine": 13
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Open Terminal and run:",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 16
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "You'll see something like:",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 18
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Copy the text inside the quotes on the **Developer ID Installer** line and paste it into **Signing identity**. The code in brackets is your Team ID.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 24
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Or click the %@ button next to the field to pick from the identities the app found.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 25
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "`-p codesigning` only lists certificates that sign apps and code, so the Installer certificate doesn't show up. `-p basic` lists every identity. `-v` hides expired, revoked and incomplete ones, so only usable identities are shown.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 29
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "To show just installer identities:",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 30
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "See the certificate's full name, team and expiry date:",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 35
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Compare with the list without `-v`. If the certificate appears there but not with `-v`, it has expired, been revoked, or its private key isn't on this Mac:",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 37
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "In **Keychain Access**, open **login › My Certificates**. A usable identity has a disclosure triangle with a private key underneath.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 39
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "In Xcode, choose **Settings › Accounts**, select your team, click **Manage Certificates…**, then **+ › Developer ID Installer**. Only the Account Holder (or an Admin with access) can create Developer ID certificates. You can also create one at developer.apple.com under **Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles**.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 43
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "If the certificate was made on another Mac, export it with its private key as a .p12 from that Mac's Keychain Access and import it here.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 44
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Confirm the signature on a built package:",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 48
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "For packages shared outside your MDM, notarize and staple them too (replace `notary` with your notarytool keychain profile):",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 50
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "The identifier is a reverse-DNS name that MDMs and `pkgutil` use to track the install, such as `com.yourcompany.teams-backgrounds`. Keep it the same across versions and raise **Version** each time you deploy new backgrounds.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 58
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Choose **Teams Backgrounds › Settings…** to remember your identifier and signing identity between sessions or set defaults.",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 26,
          "startingLine": 59
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Copy",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 24,
          "startingLine": 104
        }
      },
      {
        "comment": "",
        "key": "Copy command",
        "location": {
          "startingColumn": 23,
          "startingLine": 110
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "version": 1
}
